{"schema_version":2,"unit_id":"tag:06IY:statement","parent_tag":"06IL","chapter":"formal-defos","node_kind":"remark","risk_level":"R3","source_commit":"a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14","source_text":"Let <MATH_0001> be a predeformation functor\nsatisfying (S1) and (S2) and <MATH_0002>.\nRecall that these conditions correspond to the conditions\n(H1), (H2), and (H3) from Schlessinger's paper, see\nRemark <REF_0001>.\nNow, in the classical case (or if <MATH_0003> is separable)\nfollowing Schlessinger we introduce the notion of a hull: a <TEXTITOPEN_0001>hull<TEXTITCLOSE_0001>\nis a versal formal object <MATH_0004> such that\n<MATH_0005>\nis an isomorphism, i.e., (<REF_0002>) holds.\nThus Theorem <REF_0003> tells us\n<MATHSEG_0001> there exists a hull<MATHSEG_0002>\nin the classical case. In other words, our theorem\nrecovers Schlessinger's theorem on the existence of hulls.\n","source_status":"CURRENT","placeholders":{"MATH_0001":"$F : \\mathcal{C}_\\Lambda \\to \\textit{Sets}$","MATH_0002":"$\\dim_k TF < \\infty$","REF_0001":"\\ref{remark-compare-schlessinger-H3-pre}","MATH_0003":"$k' \\subset k$","TEXTITOPEN_0001":"{\\it ","TEXTITCLOSE_0001":"}","MATH_0004":"$\\xi \\in \\widehat{F}(R)$","MATH_0005":"$d\\underline{\\xi} : T\\underline{R}|_{\\mathcal{C}_\\Lambda} \\to TF$","REF_0002":"\\ref{equation-bijective}","REF_0003":"\\ref{theorem-miniversal-object-existence}","MATHSEG_0001":"$$\n(H1) + (H2) + (H3)\n\\Rightarrow\n\\text{","MATHSEG_0002":"}\n$$"},"render":{"prefix":"\\begin{remark}\n\\label{remark-compare-schlessinger-H3}\n","suffix":"\\end{remark}"},"math_text_regions":[{"region_id":"math/0001","delimiter_kind":"display-dollar","source":"$$\n(H1) + (H2) + (H3)\n\\Rightarrow\n\\text{ there exists a hull}\n$$","source_hash":"sha256:bef8b871851202ab76503ad8439f720210ef8fc0f3dbce25ab865e3c43a58cf9","source_byte_span":{"start":724,"end":788},"pieces":[{"kind":"locked","placeholder":"MATHSEG_0001"},{"kind":"text","slot_id":"math/0001/text/0001"},{"kind":"lock